            "date": "2026-06-11",
            "author": "mpfaffenberger",
            "subject": "fix(steering): kill input lag and add cursor-aware line editing to the Ctrl+T prompt",
            "body": "Lag: _wait_while_suspended parked on suspend_event.wait() - but that event IS set while suspended, so Event.wait() returned instantly and the loop busy-spun at 100% CPU for the entire steering prompt, hogging the GIL and lagging raw-mode input. Park on stop_event.wait(0.05) instead (genuinely unset, sleeps properly). The same bug existed copy-pasted inline in the POSIX listener fallback; both call sites now share the fixed helper (released_event is optional).",
            "theme": "tools",
            "kind": "fix",
            "impact": "notable",
            "summary": {
              "impact": "notable",
              "what": "Lag: _wait_while_suspended parked on suspend_event.wait() - but that event IS set while suspended, so Event.wait() returned instantly and the loop busy-spun at 100% CPU for the entire steering prompt, hogging the GIL and lagging raw-mode input.",
              "why_rad": "Park on stop_event.wait(0.05) instead (genuinely unset, sleeps properly).",
              "how_helps": "The same bug existed copy-pasted inline in the POSIX listener fallback; both call sites now share the fixed helper (released_event is optional)."
            },
            "files": [
              "pyproject.toml",
              "uv.lock"
            ],
            "file_count": 2,
