        "author": "weegens-aaron",
        "subject": "fix: force UTF-8 through the exec-command pipe (Windows cp1252 crash)",
        "body": "/flux/about died with UnicodeEncodeError on Windows: the exec runner spawns scripts with stdout on a pipe, so the child Python defaults its stdio to the legacy codepage (cp1252) and crashes the moment a script prints an emoji. The parent-side text=True decode mojibakes for the same reason.",
        "theme": "ux",
        "kind": "fix",
        "impact": "notable",
        "summary": {
          "impact": "notable",
          "what": "/flux/about died with UnicodeEncodeError on Windows: the exec runner spawns scripts with stdout on a pipe, so the child Python defaults its stdio to the legacy codepage (cp1252) and crashes the moment a script prints an emoji.",
          "why_rad": "The parent-side text=True decode mojibakes for the same reason.",
          "how_helps": "Your experience is smoother and more predictable."
        },
