        "author": "Andrew Tilson",
        "subject": "puppy_kennel: store /kennel toggle in puppy.cfg as single source of truth (#472)",
        "body": "The /kennel enable|disable slash commands now persist their state to puppy.cfg under the key 'kennel_enabled' instead of a separate JSON state file. Default behaviour (enabled) is unchanged; only the storage location moves. This puts the kennel toggle alongside every other user-tunable preference and lets any front-end / settings UI read and write the same value the CLI uses.",
